WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:49.791
In these eighteenth and nineteenth 
verses of the sixth chapter,

2
00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:52.666
Lord Krishna is once again shedding light

3
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:55.916
on the importance of self-restraint and balance.

4
00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:56.833
Along with this,

5
00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:58.791
he is also showing what the perfected

6
00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:02.875
form of yoga and a yogi will be like.

7
00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:12.208
When a yogi learns to control their mind 

8
00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:15.625
through continuous practice
 and discipline, then they reach a state

9
00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:18.666
where their consciousness becomes stable

10
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:25.250
and they become free from material desires.

11
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.583
This is the time when a yogi

12
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:32.666
has completely established
 themselves in yoga practice.

13
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:35.875
In the eighteenth verse, Lord Krishna clarifies

14
00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:40.250
that a true yogi not only calms the mind,

15
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:45.750
but also rises above desires 
connected to material prosperity.

16
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.375
This is that supreme state

17
00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:53.875
where the mind is not disturbed in the least 
by desires, worries, or cravings of the senses.

18
00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:59.000
In this state, the yogi becomes detached from
 all worldly entanglements.

19
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.166
And in this excellent state of yoga,

20
00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:06.208
they become focused only on their spiritual form.

21
00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:10.875
Then in the nineteenth verse, Lord Krishna 
explains this calm and stable state

22
00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:14.250
with a very beautiful metaphor.

23
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.291
He says that if air is completely absent,

24
00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:22.083
the flame of a lamp will never flicker,

25
00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:26.833
it will just keep burning 
completely stable and calm.

26
00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:32.500
The mind of a yogi absorbed in deep
 meditation is also like this –

27
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.583
stable and calm.

28
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:39.625
This metaphor shows the unwavering
 concentration and peace

29
00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.750
of a yogi's mind.

30
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.958
Ordinarily, the mind is also 
restless like a lamp's flame.

31
00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.458
The slightest wind of desires
 and entanglements blows

32
00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:52.375
and it becomes agitated.

33
00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:56.791
But a perfected yogi remains untouched
 by this worldly wind.

34
00:02:56.791 --> 00:03:01.166
They create such a cover of concentration
 around themselves

35
00:03:01.166 --> 00:03:03.875
that the wind of the world doesn't disturb them.

36
00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:09.750
And the flame of their mind keeps 
burning completely calm and stable.

37
00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.750
Here we must remember that yoga
 is not just some physical activities

38
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.541
or following some rules.

39
00:03:17.541 --> 00:03:21.041
The purpose of yoga is unwavering
 peace of mind.

40
00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:24.750
A state when the mind 
is free from worldly desires,

41
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:28.416
untouched by entanglements, calm,

42
00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:31.666
and focused only on Paramātmā.

43
00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:34.041
This is the ultimate state of yoga.

44
00:03:34.041 --> 00:03:38.416
And such a yogi is called a 'yukta' yogi.

45
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:49.041
The flame of a lamp is very
 restless and unstable,

46
00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:53.291
it flickers even in the slightest air.

47
00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:56.791
A person's mind is also like this –

48
00:03:56.791 --> 00:04:02.375
the slightest worldly wind 
blows and it becomes unstable.

49
00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:10.708
It keeps flickering in the wind of external 
circumstances, cravings, and difficulties.

50
00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:15.791
There are countless sources to disturb a person –

51
00:04:15.791 --> 00:04:18.416
thoughts of success-failure,

52
00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:21.458
worry about the future, 
craving to get something,

53
00:04:21.458 --> 00:04:24.375
someone's personal comment.

54
00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:27.125
This list is endless.

55
00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:33.208
And here's where the big mistake happens – 
a person looks for the path to their peace

56
00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:37.375
in the removal of all these.

57
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:42.916
But the truth is, neither 
will the world's problems end,

58
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:48.750
nor will materialism stop trying to tempt you.

59
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:52.583
The solution to all this must be found not outside,

60
00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:55.166
but within.

61
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:59.958
The mind must be made so stable that 
even in the wind of worldly worries

62
00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:03.916
and cravings, it doesn't get disturbed.

63
00:05:03.916 --> 00:05:08.541
Yoga is such a path to this solution,

64
00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:12.875
walking on which a person can keep their mind

65
00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:16.708
protected from the influence
of cravings and worries,

66
00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.458
keep it calm and stable.

67
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:24.625
And also, understand another thing here:

68
00:05:24.625 --> 00:05:28.833
if there's no wind, the flame won't flicker.

69
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:33.083
Similarly, if the environment around you

70
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:36.041
is not disturbing,

71
00:05:36.041 --> 00:05:39.000
the mind will also wander less.

72
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.375
Understand from these practical examples:

73
00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.750
when sitting down to do some important work,

74
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.500
you kept the phone away
 so the mind doesn't wander.

75
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.833
You kept the surrounding area organized

76
00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:55.875
so attention also remains organized.

77
00:05:55.875 --> 00:06:00.625
You reduced meeting people who disturb you.

78
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:03.708
You must have understood the point.

79
00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:07.666
There are two paths to peace: First –

80
00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.583
keep the mind stable.

81
00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:12.041
Yoga will help in this.

82
00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:16.208
Second – the wind that distracts the mind,

83
00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:21.458
meaning control the environment 
around you as much as possible.

84
00:06:21.458 --> 00:06:24.375
This will also have a positive effect.

85
00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:26.041
Think about it.

86
00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:34.708
This situation must have 
happened with you too –

87
00:06:34.708 --> 00:06:40.041
a lamp or candle's flame is flickering,

88
00:06:40.041 --> 00:06:46.541
so you made a cover with your palm around it,

89
00:06:46.541 --> 00:06:50.750
and the flame started glowing with vigor again.

90
00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:56.541
This happened because you blocked 
the effect of external wind.

91
00:06:56.541 --> 00:07:01.041
Now imagine, that flame

92
00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:08.541
is a family member's enthusiasm,
their mental state, their confidence.

93
00:07:08.541 --> 00:07:13.833
In society and family these days, 
who knows how many winds are blowing

94
00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.500
that can extinguish this flame.

95
00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:20.625
Somewhere there's competition, 
somewhere the craving for show.

96
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:25.916
Sometimes there's criticism,
sometimes professional failure.

97
00:07:25.916 --> 00:07:32.541
All these things can extinguish 
anyone's flame of confidence.

98
00:07:32.541 --> 00:07:37.250
But if all family members join hands

99
00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:43.083
and create a cover with their palms all around,

100
00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:47.833
then this flame of confidence will never flicker.

101
00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:50.541
This is the meaning of family.

102
00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:53.583
Such a secure environment

103
00:07:53.583 --> 00:07:57.958
where you can tell the state of
 your heart in times of difficulty.

104
00:07:57.958 --> 00:08:00.583
Where you get love, get help.

105
00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:06.208
Where there are many palms to
 save your extinguishing flame.

106
00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:09.125
If the family environment remains like this,

107
00:08:09.125 --> 00:08:14.000
no external problem can break a person.

108
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.750
If someone in the family is going through
difficulty, listen to them peacefully.

109
00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.125
If possible, give some suggestion.

110
00:08:22.125 --> 00:08:25.041
And even if you can't give suggestions,

111
00:08:25.041 --> 00:08:31.375
just your time and company
 can increase someone's courage.

112
00:08:31.375 --> 00:08:34.916
There are already so many 
problems in external society,

113
00:08:34.916 --> 00:08:41.000
so at least try to make 
the home environment positive.

114
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.500
Where there's no criticism,
 but sympathy and empathy.

115
00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.708
Where there's no discord, but love.

116
00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:50.625
And this is only possible

117
00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:55.041
when you water your family 
with spiritual teachings

118
00:08:55.041 --> 00:08:59.125
and focus them toward a supreme purpose.

119
00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:06.666
In the professional setting,

120
00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:12.208
your mind is also like 
the burning flame of a lamp.

121
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:15.000
The purpose of this flame is

122
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.791
to keep the path of your progress bright,

123
00:09:17.791 --> 00:09:20.875
so that you can clearly see the path to success.

124
00:09:20.875 --> 00:09:26.166
But in the professional world, 
there are countless winds all around –

125
00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:30.916
of stress, competition, and greed.

126
00:09:30.916 --> 00:09:36.583
Because of these winds, 
this flame of the mind often flickers,

127
00:09:36.583 --> 00:09:38.458
the path becomes unclear,

128
00:09:38.458 --> 00:09:41.750
and the person wanders

129
00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.250
from their purpose.

130
00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:47.208
For instance, you're working well,

131
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:50.458
but then you saw someone else succeed.

132
00:09:50.458 --> 00:09:54.625
You got disturbed and 
now leaving your work process,

133
00:09:54.625 --> 00:09:57.791
you started imitating them.

134
00:09:57.791 --> 00:10:00.500
Or you were on the path of truth,

135
00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.833
but seeing someone amass
 wealth through unethical ways,

136
00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:07.583
you too were tempted toward that wrong path.

137
00:10:07.583 --> 00:10:13.250
There are many such examples where a person
 wanders from their path.

138
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:16.333
If you let the flame of the mind flicker,

139
00:10:16.333 --> 00:10:18.833
you will also keep wandering futilely.

140
00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:23.125
Therefore, try to keep the mind concentrated.

141
00:10:23.125 --> 00:10:26.708
For this, three things are important:

142
00:10:26.708 --> 00:10:31.041
First – if you keep working
 with quality continuously,

143
00:10:31.041 --> 00:10:33.291
success will definitely come.

144
00:10:33.291 --> 00:10:39.166
Second – professional life is 
not a competition with limited time.

145
00:10:39.166 --> 00:10:41.541
Everyone's time will come.

146
00:10:41.541 --> 00:10:45.250
If today is someone else's, 
tomorrow will be yours too.

147
00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.583
Don't get disturbed by others' success.

148
00:10:48.583 --> 00:10:55.708
Third thing – keep trying to keep the mind
 concentrated and calm.

149
00:10:55.708 --> 00:10:58.500
Self-reflection, meditation, yoga,

150
00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:04.416
and yes, the Bhagavad Gita
 will also help you in this.

151
00:11:04.416 --> 00:11:07.125
Save the flame of the mind from flickering

152
00:11:07.125 --> 00:11:11.625
and just keep moving 
firmly on the path of action.
